                <pb facs="0444" n="374" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg374"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2404: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Dearing</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-17T14:00:00-05:00">December 17, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>72. Your 126, December 13, 11 p.m., paragraph 5. You may advise the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs orally in the strictest confidence that <pb facs="0445" n="375"
                        xml:id="pg375"/> we have expressed our interest in this matter to the
                    Colombian Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
